langcode":"en","revision_timestamp":"2026-02-10T23:15:19+00:00","status":true,"title":"Pipeline to Production in Minutes: How a Leading P\u0026C Insurer Achieved End-to-End DevOps on Databricks","created":"2026-02-10T23:15:19+00:00","changed":"2026-07-14T17:15:24+00:00","promote":true,"sticky":false,"default_langcode":true,"revision_translation_affected":true,"moderation_state":null,"metatag":[{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"name":"title","content":"Pipeline to Production in Minutes: How a Leading P\u0026C Insurer Achieved End-to-End DevOps on Databricks | Databricks"}},{"tag":"link","attributes":{"rel":"canonical","href":"https://microsites.databricks.com/dataaisummit2026agendaitem/pipeline-production-minutes-how-leading-pc-insurer-achieved-end-end"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"property":"og:type","content":"website"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"property":"og:url","content":"https://microsites.databricks.com/dataaisummit2026agendaitem/pipeline-production-minutes-how-leading-pc-insurer-achieved-end-end"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"property":"og:title","content":"Pipeline to Production in Minutes: How a Leading P\u0026C Insurer Achieved End-to-End DevOps on Databricks | Databricks"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"property":"og:image","content":"https://www.databricks.com/dataaisummit/sites/default/files/2026-02/dais26-og-1200x628.jpg"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"property":"og:locale","content":"en"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"property":"article:publisher","content":"https://www.facebook.com/databricksinc/"}},{"tag":"meta","attributes":{"name":"twitter:card","content":"summary_large_image"}}],"path":{"alias":"/dataaisummit2026agendaitem/pipeline-production-minutes-how-leading-pc-insurer-achieved-end-end","pid":17776,"langcode":"en"},"content_translation_source":"und","content_translation_outdated":false,"body":null,"field_agenda_body":{"value":"\u003cp\u003eP\u0026C insurance data platforms must deliver analytics rapidly while meeting stringent governance and regulatory requirements. Although Databricks is widely adopted as the analytics backbone, many P\u0026C organizations continue to struggle with inconsistent deployments, manual promotions and fragmented DevOps practices.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis lightning talk demonstrates how a P\u0026C organization implemented true end-to-end DevOps on Databricks using Asset Bundles, Databricks Apps and GitHub Actions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLearn how a Git-driven, declarative deployment model uses Asset Bundles to package notebooks, workflows and DLT pipelines with environment-aware configuration, enabling consistent promotion across multiple environments, while GitHub Actions orchestrates CI/CD pipelines for validation, automated deployment and auditability.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe session highlights how Databricks Apps are integrated into the same pipeline to operationalize analytics use cases as secure, production-ready data product governed by Unity Catalog.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\n","format":"basic_html","processed":"\u003cp\u003eP\u0026amp;C insurance data platforms must deliver analytics rapidly while meeting stringent governance and regulatory requirements. Although Databricks is widely adopted as the analytics backbone, many P\u0026amp;C organizations continue to struggle with inconsistent deployments, manual promotions and fragmented DevOps practices.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis lightning talk demonstrates how a P\u0026amp;C organization implemented true end-to-end DevOps on Databricks using Asset Bundles, Databricks Apps and GitHub Actions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLearn how a Git-driven, declarative deployment model uses Asset Bundles to package notebooks, workflows and DLT pipelines with environment-aware configuration, enabling consistent promotion across multiple environments, while GitHub Actions orchestrates CI/CD pipelines for validation, automated deployment and auditability.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe session highlights how Databricks Apps are integrated into the same pipeline to operationalize analytics use cases as secure, production-ready data product governed by Unity Catalog.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr\u003e"},"field_agenda_code_id":"D26L1128","field_agenda_duration":"20","field_agenda_ends":"2026-06-16T20:30:00+00:00","field_agenda_starts":"2026-06-16T20:10:00+00:00","field_agenda_unique_id":"1766784520387001PY2e","field_metatags":null,"field_price":null,"field_slides_url":"https://microsites.databricks.com/sites/default/files/dais/2026/D26L1128.pdf","field_video_chunks":[],"field_video_transcript":null,"field_video_url":"https://cdnapisec.kaltura.com/p/6501692/embedPlaykitJs/uiconf_id/57932942?autoembed=true\u0026targetId=kaltura_player_326743298\u0026entry_id=1_c7unfkab","links":{"self":{"href":"https://microsites.databricks.com/jsonapi/node/dataaisummit2026_agenda_item/d29db724-3e23-48aa-b25b-e5752dcf47dd?resourceVersion=id%3A25385"},"working-copy":{"href":"https://microsites.databricks.com/jsonapi/node/dataaisummit2026_agenda_item/d29db724-3e23-48aa-b25b-e5752dcf47dd?resourceVersion=rel%3Aworking-copy"}},"node_type":{"type":"node_type--node_type","id":"02af01b1-e063-4d57-a525-a7a8f2f9b968","resourceIdObjMeta":{"drupal_internal__target_id":"dataaisummit2026_agenda_item"}},"revision_uid":null,"uid":null,"field_agenda_category":[{"type":"taxonomy_term--dataaisummit_agenda_category","id":"dd70980